node_modules/
.superpowers/
# Codex worker logs, prompts and ledgers (orchestration state, not source)
.kiln/
.kiln-shots/
# The owner's per-slot release approval is machine-local state bound to a source digest;
# it is never committed, so a stale record cannot travel with the repo.
release-approval.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Promo codes for any slot's promotions, at any depth. A code is a free unlock of whatever
# the slot sells, so a batch is a pile of giveaways and a repository history is the wrong
# place for one. The slot's own `.gitignore` and the scaffold's both carry these two names;
# this entry is the backstop for a code file that lands in the repository root instead, so
# the protection does not depend on which folder the download happened to reach.
promo-codes.csv
promotion_codes.csv
*.jks
*.keystore
google-services.json
play-service-account.json
**/local.properties
**/.gradle/
**/build/
**/.idea/
**/*.iml
**/captures/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
# JVM crash dumps land in the project root, not in build/, so they need their own rule:
# an out-of-memory Gradle daemon writes hs_err_pid<pid>.log beside the build files.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
.tmp-android-skills/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
